Let the browser cache uploaded media

Firebase Storage stamps `private, max-age=0` on anything uploaded without
explicit metadata, so nothing we upload is ever cached — a returning
visitor re-downloads the whole hero video, and every project still, on
every visit.

Uploaded objects are immutable in practice: the key carries an upload
timestamp and replacing a file writes a new object under a new name. So
they can be cached indefinitely.

Both upload paths now set `public, max-age=31536000, immutable`.

Applies to newly uploaded files only; existing objects keep the old
header until they are re-uploaded or their metadata is edited in the
Firebase console.

